.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-01T09:19:36-07:00","id":1494090,"title":"","content":"The bloodline I like the least is The True Brujah. Mostly I couldn't understand how Temporis fit in the VTM theme at all. That power would be better suited in Changeling or Mage in all seriousness and there cold emotionless demeanors didn't appeal to me.<br /> <br /> Now for the bloodline that I had a soft spot for was The Old Clan Tzmisce was dedicated lore collectors and problematic defenders of there fiefdoms and holding true what they wanted in seeking potentiol new clan members and made no pretensions in pretending to be human anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T03:44:47-07:00","id":1494195,"title":"","content":"Much like with <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\">Sergeant Brother</a></b> said previously, the name Nagaraja always bothered me - in my own games, it's the title of the foremost among the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shesha\" target=\"_blank\">Followers of Shesha</a> in a domain, meaning also that in areas where the clan has considerable cultural mileage the title has become synonymous with Prince or Primogen and may be used as either even by non-sheshite kindred across domains in Vietnam, Laos or Cambodia among other countries.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the bloodline of flesh-eating necromancers is known under a number of different names in certain parts of the world.<br /> <br /> - In India and nations that have been culturally influenced by it through the ages, they have been called <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pishacha\" target=\"_blank\">Pishacha</a></b> for centuries and perhaps more.<br /> - Meanwhile in the middle east and much of the arab-speaking world <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghoul\" target=\"_blank\">Ghul</a></b> was used for centuries but has been slowly but steadily replaced by <b>Galla</b>, out of either pretensions to ancient millenia old origins or want of distancing themselves of a term increasingly associated with vitae-empowered thralls.<br /> - In the western world two names have gained milleage as representatives of major groups of the bloodline: the <b>Nihilistics</b>, a group with cultic/secret society underpinings not unlike the Tremere (and some theorize, formed from either a splinter group or as a sort of foil/response to the Warlocks) widespread through much of central and eastern europe from unclear beginnings somewhere in german-speaking countries or the russian empire between 17th to 19th centuries.<br /> - And in the British Isles it's the <b>Dunsirn </b>family of banker-cannibals that has gained traction, at least in part due to support from Mithras as a foil to Tremere and Giovanni both, with something of a presence in a number of Ventrue-ruled domains across the english-speaking world where relations of Blue Bloods with either Warlocks or Necromancers tend toward unfriendly.<br /> <br /> (In my games, due to me sticking to my own pre-clanbook Queen of Damned-inspired personal take of them, the idea of Giovanni &quot;branch families&quot; made no real sense, so i made them into rival families/traditions of death-magicians causing the venetians much grief instead. Redoing the Dunsirn as &quot;Nagaraja&quot; was just too convenient and fun to ignore - and in fact is what got me going into this remake of the families in the first place)<br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, the division of bloodlines in multiple enclaves of quasi-clan weight within a certain niche/region, semi- to fully independent from each other and sometimes with their own culture and particular mythology/origin tales is one of the major factors in the divide between clans and bloodlines: numbers and a sense of common identity (lacking on the later, obviously), that kind of contributes to make their numbers seem even smaller, since a Dunsirn <b><i>might</i> </b>see a common identity with a Nihilistic as &quot;distant relatives/brothers in the Way&quot; and vice-versa depending on situation and individual, but the same happening with a Galla - or Pishacha - could be much less probable. Damn, they might accuse the Dunsirn of being a thieving pretender of a dirty british diablerist while at it!<br /> <br /> Much of the same can go, for example, with Marconius' Kiasyd line in Alsace x the much older Dokkalfar from the scandinavian countries x the Moon Eyed People in their warrens within &amp; under the Appalachia since the coming of the Cherokee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-17-2024, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}